# The R36S's kernel config: the GKD Pixel 2's (board/px2/linux.config, from
# ROCKNIX's RK3326 config cut down to what the Pixel 2 uses) with what the
# R36S needs and the Pixel 2 does not. scripts/build-r36s-kernel.sh merges it
# in (the kernel's merge_config.sh) and says if a line here did not hold.
# The same chip (RK3326, which Linux calls PX30), the same RK817 for power
# and sound, the same Panfrost, the same ROCKNIX joypad driver (its
# singleadc one, here with the sticks' analog mux) and generic-dsi panel
# driver: all already in the Pixel 2's.

# The panel its device tree names (rk3326-gameconsole-r3xs.dtsi):
# "gameconsole,r36s-panel", an ST7703 whose mode and init sequence ROCKNIX's
# panel patch adds (board/px2/patches/linux/2-rk3326-001-panel-updates.patch,
# r36s_desc). The Pixel 2's config leaves the ST7703 driver out. The other
# panels R36S units ship with go through generic-dsi and a device tree
# overlay instead (docs/devices/r36s.md, "Panels").
CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_SITRONIX_ST7703=y
